WEBVTT

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.290
<i>After defeating the Spectre Nemesis,</i>

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.610
<i>Seth had another encounter with Grimm.</i>

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.980
<i>Grimm told him about the Luchorpan,</i>

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.680
<i>the inn where Melie and Doc were staying,</i>

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.340
<i>and Seth headed there himself.</i>

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.750
<b>Luchorpan Inn</b>

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:02.500
Who the heck is here at this hour?

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:05.500
Seth!

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.930
H-Hi.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.740
H-How'd you know we were here?!

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:12.130
Listen... Is Melie here?

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:16.130
M-Melie is... asleep already.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.630
She is?

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:20.760
Just leave! Leave quick!

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.790
Whoa! What's the deal?!

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.890
Leave right now! Leave at Mach speed!

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:22.890
C'mon, Doc!

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.180
But why?!

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:27.540
Damn it! It's for your own good, okay?!

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:28.270
Huh?!

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.650
I just want to apologize to her!

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:36.150
Apologize? For what?

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:39.500
Melie...

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:17.050
<b>Silent Rain, Distant Hearts 
-Rain-</b>

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:16.070
<i>"Silent Rain, Distant Hearts."</i>

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:23.130
Apologize? For what?

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.260
Melie...

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:29.910
What made you decide 
to come see us now?

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:33.300
What made me... I mean...

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:37.290
I left Artemis
 without telling you guys.

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:39.190
So—

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.580
Oh, that?

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.110
In that case,
 there's no need to apologize.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.180
You can go now.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:47.890
Wait! What's going on?

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:49.850
I have a very busy day tomorrow.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:53.520
Y-You're angry because 
I left without telling you, right?

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:54.830
I believe I told you that I'm not.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.420
Well, then...

00:03:57.490 --> 00:04:00.610
What <i>are</i> you so angry about?

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:02.380
I'm not angry.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.180
Yes, you are!

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.500
I'm really not angry at all.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:10.180
I just envy you. That's all.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.180
Seth, it must be nice to be you.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:14.580
Huh?

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.770
You move on to the next thing so easily.

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:23.750
We did a lot of things together
 after you arrived in Artemis, didn't we?

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:25.320
Yeah...

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.810
We had tea at Kettle Coffee,

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:32.080
accepted jobs from Master Lord Majesty...
 So many things.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.790
Y-Yeah...

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:37.860
Lots of those things were scary or sad,

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.570
but I thought the three of us 
made it through them together.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:44.340
The time we spent together was short,

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:47.930
but I thought of us as a team...
 as friends.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:53.850
But it wasn't like that for you,
 was it, Seth?

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:55.570
Melie...

00:04:56.110 --> 00:05:01.190
We didn't mean to you
 what you meant to us, did we?

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:07.740
You have nothing to say?

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:09.660
Well, that's fine.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:13.490
But that must mean
 it was all my own misunderstanding.

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:14.750
You're wrong!

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:19.250
You guys... are important to me.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.610
But... that's why I...

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:26.170
I didn't want
 to put you through any trouble.

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:29.260
Trouble? What trouble?

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:31.640
Well, I mean...

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:34.530
I wanted to strengthen my magic more.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:37.230
I wanted to become a powerful sorcerer.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:41.650
That's why I wanted to go
 and see the Knights-sorcerers.

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:45.300
But you disappeared without a word.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:51.280
I thought if I told you guys about this,
 you'd follow me.

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:57.040
But if you were with me,
 there was no telling what might happen to you.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:01.010
Plus... I'm not sure why,

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:03.990
but those Thaumaturge guys are after me.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.810
And I...

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:10.930
I didn't want to put you guys in danger.

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.060
Putting aside Doc in his current state,

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:16.670
I am not a child.

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:19.290
I can take care of myself.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:19.890
But—

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:23.500
Besides, even if the worst 
were to happen to me,

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:26.320
it would be my own responsibility.

00:06:26.890 --> 00:06:29.850
I had no intention of laying the blame on you.

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:33.650
But you didn't trust us.

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:37.430
That's why you came to
 this town alone, isn't it?

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.770
No, it's not... But...

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:42.960
But?

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.750
That's why...

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.210
Melie...

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:47.330
Doc...

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:55.100
I didn't want you two with me.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:01.600
That's going too far.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:06.370
It's not just the Nemesis and
 the Inquisition that are dangerous.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:08.490
It's me!

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.570
I don't know when I might lose control again.

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:16.620
And if you guys are around me when I do...

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:17.610
If we are?

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:19.260
Are you serious?

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:23.310
Did you forget what happened to me 
when I fought the Thaumaturges?!

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:26.530
I remember well how scary it was.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:30.340
Then you should understand!

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:33.560
When I lose control,
 I don't know what's what.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:35.210
I can't tell friend from foe!

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:40.190
So in the end, you're saying
 that we're not strong enough, right?

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.650
That's not the point!

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:46.320
I'm so inexperienced and useless

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:50.150
that all I could do if you went berserk
 would be to lose hopelessly?

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:53.410
I don't think either 
of you is inexperienced!

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.120
But you don't have any need for us.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:59.240
That's not true!
 I just don't want to hurt you!

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:02.500
When I can't even control what I do,

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.000
I can't be around my friends—

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.590
What's that supposed to mean?

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:13.290
You're not allowed to have friends
 if you're not 100% in control of yourself?

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:17.890
You're not allowed ask others 
for help when you're in trouble?

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:20.640
You're just supposed to be alone forever?!

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:24.390
Since my curse turns me into someone else,
 does that go for me, too?!

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:25.940
Of course, right?

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:31.190
Someone who might hurt others
 without realizing it is terrifying, right?!

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:34.660
Someone like that can't
 make friends so easily, right?!

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:40.790
I know that better than anyone.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:48.820
I was always alone because of my curse.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:52.810
Like there was a huge gap between me
 and everyone else,

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:55.030
because I couldn't control
 my other personality.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.570
It ruined my entire life.

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:01.780
But still, I always wished...

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:05.150
that someone would stay by my side.

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:08.860
That someone would stop me 
from doing something crazy.

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:14.580
If I had someone to stop me 
from doing something crazy...

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:21.240
maybe that wouldn't have happened to Venelope.

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:29.150
I had finally found someone 
who understood my curse,

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:33.230
my pain, from the bottom of their heart.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:37.550
Someone I could trust,
 who trusted me in return.

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:40.420
At least, that's what I thought.

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:05.740
I'm sorry for that nonsensical outburst.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:07.300
Melie...

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:11.140
Don't bother.
 It's not as if I want you to comfort me.

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:13.980
I don't want your sympathy, either.

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:18.810
I wouldn't know, but maybe

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:22.900
the way you live is the right way,
 after all.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:27.770
If you don't get close to anyone... 
If you avoid getting involved...

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:31.450
I suppose you'll never get hurt.

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:37.390
But I wanted a friend
 who would worry with me,

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:40.890
who would walk by my side.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:47.590
It's not about
 who's right and who's wrong.

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:52.960
I guess the two of us
 just wanted different things.

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:54.960
Goodbye.

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:17.980
<b>[Luchorpan] 
A cheap lodging in Caislean Merlin.
 A place where many have stayed, and missed each other...</b>

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:34.270
I've never seen Melie cry like that before.

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:54.570
You know,
 I told Melie she shouldn't come here.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:57.860
But she wouldn't listen to me.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:00.130
She said she wanted

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:03.390
to strengthen her magic and prove
 that she could handle things on her own.

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:10.500
Apparently, she's had a few chances
 to work with other people in the past.

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:14.390
But every time she did,
 her curse messed everything up.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:18.430
Melie waited all her life to meet

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:22.060
someone like you,
 who doesn't care about curses.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:24.470
But...

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:28.510
I left her.

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:31.370
Even if it wasn't your intention,

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:36.780
this ended the same way it did
 with everyone else who left her.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:42.330
So try not to blame her for it.

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:46.530
I would never blame her.

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:48.540
I see.

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:56.540
Seth, what are you going to do now?

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:58.750
Do you have somewhere to go?

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.450
I'll be fine.

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:08.020
Even I have places I can go.

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:09.940
Really?

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:13.680
That's good, then.

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:24.350
Well, I'm heading back in.

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:25.320
See you.

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:33.230
What <i>am</i> I going to do now?

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.340
This is...

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.020
Oh, right.

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:15.500
Excuse me...

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:28.800
Only three?

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:29.800
Okay, then!

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:30.750
Deine!

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:41.020
Wow...

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.740
Egwil!

00:14:56.620 --> 00:15:00.120
All right, who's been peeping in here?

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:03.250
Outsiders are forbidden 
to enter at this hour!

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:06.250
Oh... Um...

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:07.510
What?

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:08.110
Hey.

00:15:08.110 --> 00:15:11.380
Look at you! You're soaked!

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:16.390
Sheesh... What were you doing
 out in the rain dressed like that?

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:19.600
Mind if I stay in here 
while it's raining?

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:23.270
Oh, I suppose not. Here, use this.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:24.660
Thanks.

00:15:27.890 --> 00:15:29.220
It reeks of livestock!

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:30.530
No complaints!

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:34.490
By the way,
 I left my stuff here earlier today.

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:36.410
Oh, yeah. Just a sec.

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.230
Let's see.

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:42.070
Oh, here it is!
 Lulu was using it as a pillow.

00:15:42.070 --> 00:15:43.980
Lulu?

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:47.050
Oh, from the, "Lulu is napping," password...

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:49.130
You haven't met her, have you?

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.050
I'll introduce you.

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:54.470
This is Lulu.
 She takes care of my dragon.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:58.420
She also trains with me

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:00.910
and helps me out in all kinds of ways.

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:04.140
She's what you'd call
 an irreplaceable partner.

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:07.010
Uh-huh! Now, then...

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:08.820
Yoink!

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.700
Here's your stuff back.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.140
Th-Thanks...

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:19.490
Anyway, she's been asleep all this time, huh?

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:22.710
Is that what her curse is?

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:26.710
Um... W-Well, yeah.

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:28.500
Something like that.

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:30.010
Huh...

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:32.170
So, Ocoho, what's your curse?

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:34.910
E-Excuse me?! What are you even asking?!

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:36.470
I just met you!

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:37.620
That's rude!

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:40.600
Huh? Isn't that being a little too sensitive?

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:44.290
What are you talking about?!
 That's an extremely private subject!

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.090
Oh, I know!

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:50.730
I bet your curse
 makes you not listen to people!

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:52.090
Huh?!

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:54.490
You just keep getting ruder and ruder!

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:56.920
Wrong, huh? Oh, then I bet—

00:16:56.920 --> 00:16:59.770
Ugh! Help me, Draccoon!

00:16:59.770 --> 00:17:01.380
Cover my ears!

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:04.890
No! I said "cover," not "cuddle"!

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:07.070
I just want you to cover my ears!

00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:09.060
O-Okay, okay, I get it.

00:17:07.070 --> 00:17:11.500
I said stop! This is not what I meant!

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:11.500
I'll stop talking about your curse.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:17.500
I can tell you're not used to
 the way things work here.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:19.140
Where were you up until now?

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.570
Before I came here, I was in Artemis.

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:24.930
Before that,
 I lived in Pompo Hills for a while.

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:28.020
You came all the way
 to Caislean Merlin from there?

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:29.150
What for?

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:31.520
I'm looking for Radiant.

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:34.780
Radiant? Why are you looking for that?

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.500
So I can destroy it.

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:41.300
And I heard that the knights here
 were looking for Radiant, too,

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:43.300
but it looks like that was a mistake.

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:46.940
It sure was. That was a long time ago.

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:51.410
So I have no choice but to get
 into the castle archive after all.

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:53.830
The archive is heavily guarded.

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:56.450
Myr?!

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:58.770
When did you sneak in?!

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:02.700
What are you doing?
 And why do you always come in here?!

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:06.810
I'm just getting out of the rain.
 It's pouring out there.

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:08.690
Hey!

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.730
Don't eat Draccoon's food!

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:13.520
Just go back to your wife already!

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:18.570
I can't! She gave me the boot,
 because she thinks I cheated on her!

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:19.810
You? Cheat?

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:21.580
Ha! Is that a joke?

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:23.080
What are you saying?

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:26.720
I've got myself a mistress or two, you know!

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:29.650
Um, I should really...

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:31.490
Just listen to the song I wrote
 with them in mind!

00:18:31.490 --> 00:18:32.670
Ahem!

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:35.100
<i>Two ripe fruits...</i>

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:37.340
No! Help me, Draccoon!

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:38.530
<i>A gentle breeze makes the fruit sway,</i>

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:39.220
Cover my ears!

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:41.320
<i>and I couldn't be in higher spirits...</i>

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:44.140
No! I said "cover," not "cuddle"!

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:45.610
<i>Hm, hm, hm, la, la, la... 
Th-Th-This fruit is so tender...</i>

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.350
Stop singing that filthy song!

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:50.750
Hey! You could help me out, you know!

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:52.820
H-Huh?

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:55.740
<i>He's still an awful singer.</i>

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:56.860
Where do you think you're going?

00:18:56.860 --> 00:19:00.240
Isn't there something 
you need to say to me?

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:04.890
Okay, I'm sorry about what happened.

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:08.040
It was my fault you got yelled at
 by that old bearded dude.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:10.750
I don't care about that! 
What I mean is...

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.090
Tell me!

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:13.750
Tell you what?

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:20.250
How did you gather that insane amount 
of Fantasia when I used Cromen?

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:21.420
Tell me!

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:24.680
Huh? I didn't do anything.

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:26.890
Didn't you do all that yourself?

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:28.430
No, I didn't!

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:33.810
I hate to admit it, but I can't gather 
that much Fantasia on my own.

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:37.330
How do you do that? Tell me!

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:40.900
But... I don't know how I do it, either.

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:42.130
Really?

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:42.990
Yeah.

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:47.290
At least be my sparring partner, then!

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:49.950
But you were doing fine 
by yourself earlier.

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:52.310
That's not enough!

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:54.830
I'm not great at defensive fighting,

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:58.420
but Lord Brangoire put me 
on the defense squad.

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:01.580
So I want to beef up 
my offensive strength

00:20:01.580 --> 00:20:04.930
and show him
 what I'm really capable of!

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:10.770
Sorry, but I've got my hands full 
with my own problems right now.

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:12.750
Aw, man...

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:15.490
Let's make a deal, then!

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:18.690
I'll look into Radiant for you!

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:21.170
Ocoho, you can get into the archive?

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:24.530
Well, not the archive,
 but I can get into the library!

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:28.030
There might be some books in there 
with information on Radiant!

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:30.540
Radiant...

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:33.660
Please! I don't have much time 
before the ordination ceremony!

00:20:33.660 --> 00:20:37.180
I really want to be a Knight-sorcerer,
 no matter what!

00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:39.050
It's been my dream forever!

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:45.180
Just think of this as fate! 
Okay? Please, help me out!

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:50.060
You're not allowed to have friends
 if you're not 100% in control of yourself?

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:54.020
You're not allowed ask others 
for help when you're in trouble?

00:20:55.700 --> 00:20:59.860
I really think
 it'd be better for me to be alone.

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:01.670
But...

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:04.890
I do need your help,

00:21:05.310 --> 00:21:08.370
and if I can help
 make your dream come true...

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:10.080
Then...

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:13.710
I'll do my best, along with you.

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:16.210
Yes! Thank you!

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:20.050
Then we'll get up at five every morning 
and train for two and a half hours!

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:21.370
G-Get up at five?!

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:25.020
And I have drills during the day, 
but I'm free in the evening!

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:27.660
So we'll just train
 until one of us goes down!

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:28.370
Huh?!

00:21:28.370 --> 00:21:31.660
You can't become a Knight-sorcerer 
if you don't do that much.

00:21:34.150 --> 00:21:35.960
All right, fine.

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:38.140
I'll go find a place to stay

00:21:38.140 --> 00:21:40.630
and come here in the mornings and evenings.

00:21:40.630 --> 00:21:42.870
You don't have a place to sleep?

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:44.450
Why don't you live here, then?

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:45.650
Huh? I can?

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:48.820
Sure! Just make sure no one finds out,
 and it'll be fine.

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:52.110
I'm sure Draccoon will make a great bed!

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:56.330
Thanks! That helps a lot!

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:59.500
Looking forward to working with you, Seth!

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:02.090
Yeah, same to you!

00:22:24.310 --> 00:22:27.790
That dream... again?

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:29.990
To Be Continued

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:20.790
<b>Next Time</b>

00:24:01.170 --> 00:24:04.850
<i>When Seth sneaks into the castle,
 something seems off.</i>

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:07.580
<i>It's his first time in the castle,</i>

00:24:07.580 --> 00:24:10.260
<i>but he's familiar with it,
 because of the dreams he's had every night.</i>

00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:14.020
<i>When he arrives at the location 
his dreams led him to,</i>

00:24:14.020 --> 00:24:18.470
<i>Seth meets a mysterious young man
 who's terrified of Piodon.</i>

00:24:19.430 --> 00:24:22.790
<i>Next time on <i>Radiant</i>,
"His Name Is."</i>

00:24:20.790 --> 00:24:25.020
<b>His Name Is 
-Diabal-</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>End</b>
